1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,500
Hi, we're Hyeonmin Choi and Jaewu Yoo.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:09,800
This is DropPDF, a web app that converts files to and from PDF right in your browser.

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:14,500
Nothing to install, and nothing is uploaded.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,500
I just drag my files in: a Word report, an Excel sheet,

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,500
a ZIP of trip photos, and a PDF brochure.

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,500
Each row shows what it will become.

7
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:31,500
For a PDF, I pick the output format right on the row:

8
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,000
Word, PowerPoint, images, or text.

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,500
I can convert just one file.

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,600
I click Convert on the report, and it's saved right away.

11
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:48,500
Here's the PDF it made.

12
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,200
Or I convert everything at once with Convert all.

13
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:00,000
The ZIP of photos became a single PDF,

14
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:04,500
one photo per page.

15
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:09,000
The brochure PDF became a Word file.

16
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:15,200
Here's the preview,

17
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,800
and here it is open in Word.

18
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:21,400
I can type right here.

19
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,300
The text is still editable,

20
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,300
and the photos and background stay in place.

21
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,500
Need slides instead?

22
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:32,500
I switch the format to PowerPoint and click Convert again,

23
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,000
with no re-upload.

24
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:41,400
Here it is in PowerPoint.

25
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:45,000
Every result is saved in the Library, even after I close the browser.

26
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:47,500
I can search and filter,

27
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:53,500
preview a file,

28
00:01:53,600 --> 00:02:00,500
rename it and add a memo,

29
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:08,100
send the original back to convert into another format,

30
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:12,000
and delete what I don't need.

31
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,400
There's also Delete all to clear everything.

32
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,500
That's DropPDF: drop your files, convert,

33
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:25,000
and keep everything in one library.

34
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Thanks for watching!

